{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WuKongIM/WuKongIM/pulls/1029","id":4974914456,"node_id":"PR_kwDOJgfwyc8AAAABKIcrmA","html_url":"https://github.com/WuKongIM/WuKongIM/pull/1029","diff_url":"https://github.com/WuKongIM/WuKongIM/pull/1029.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/WuKongIM/WuKongIM/pull/1029.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WuKongIM/WuKongIM/issues/1029","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WuKongIM/WuKongIM/pulls/1029/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WuKongIM/WuKongIM/pulls/1029/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WuKongIM/WuKongIM/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WuKongIM/WuKongIM/issues/1029/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WuKongIM/WuKongIM/statuses/c4954c6a638080e6a915ecec305a3381f4afd9a0","number":1029,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"fix(presence): isolate cold UID recovery and diagnose checkpoint failures","user":{"login":"tangtaoit","id":3895878,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM4OTU4Nzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3895878?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tangtaoit","html_url":"https://github.com/tangtaoit","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tangtaoit/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tangtaoit/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tangtaoit/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tangtaoit/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tangtaoit/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tangtaoit/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tangtaoit/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tangtaoit/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tangtaoit/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Cold presence recovery currently holds a coarse hash lane across owner I/O. An unrelated cold UID in that lane can wait behind the first request despite having its own authority proof to recover. Replace lane ownership with exact UID and distributed-authority flights, publish newly owned proofs before joining prior flights, and preserve Directory fencing, eviction semantics, existing retries and the four-call owner gate.\n\nAdmission is bounded to four leader cohorts, 2,048 retained keys and 128 MiB of registry-owned UID clones, with 32 MiB per newly owned subset. The original 512-UID/256-target packing fits maximum stored identities; oversized arbitrary cold lookup strings return typed not-ready. Flights retain status rather than routes, and successful callers reread Directory.\n\nAlso identify metadata-checkpoint finalization rejections through closed diagnostic reasons while preserving accounting, retry/deadline behavior, incomplete-report failures and prior product observations. This diagnostic change does not repair or reclassify the previously invalid report.\n\nValidation:\n- Tests-first controlled isolation regressions: old implementation produced 13 behavioral failures; the unchanged focused tests pass after the change.\n- Complete presence/runtime packages pass normally and under race (106 test events each); four production owner-adapter recovery contracts pass under race.\n- Complete chat-lifecycle/CLI benchmark packages pass (871 top-level tests / 1,685 test events); focused diagnostic race checks pass.\n- Named formatting/FLOW checks pass. Independent Standards and Spec reviews have no remaining findings; the initial P3 documentation clarification and its closure are retained.\n- Exact-source native process diagnostic retained the same 10,000-user/2,000-group distribution, seed, 500 SEND/s config and gates. It still failed: terminal SEND=ACK 10,502, zero first-attempt failures/rejections, one sampled expiry. Finalization is now specifically `meta_checkpoint/metrics_fetch`; CLI remains harness-invalid, exit 8, with no final report. All owned processes and 64 ports were cleared. This validates neither a loss fix nor the full 120-second window; the cloud rehearsal root cause remains open.\n\nThe released cloud rehearsal had message loss and remains unqualified. This PR does not publish a release or authorize another paid run.\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-10-22T22:22:51Z","updated_at":"2026-10-22T22:34:38Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"15289a0a91d1b858db667f7783955d022f965913","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"WuKongIM:codex/v3-local-presence-candidate","ref":"codex/v3-local-presence-candidate","repo":{"id":638054601,"node_id":"R_kgDOJgfwyQ","name":"WuKongIM","full_name":"WuKongIM/WuKongIM","owner":{"login":"WuKongIM","id":132860831,"node_id":"O_kgDOB-tLnw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/132860831?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WuKongIM","html_url":"https://github.com/WuKongIM","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WuKongIM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WuKongIM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WuKongIM/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WuKongIM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WuKongIM/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WuKongIM/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WuKongIM/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WuKongIM/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WuKongIM/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"private":false,"fork":false,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"description":"More than just IM 不只是即时通讯(IM)","homepage":"https://docs.githubim.com","language":"Go","visibility":"public","is_template":false,"topics":["agent","chat","im"